-- Old Age Security Act, PART II, section 15: spouses and common-law partners. Piece oa2.
--
-- Section 15 does three kinds of work. It puts duties on the applicant (state whether you have a spouse; tell the
-- Minister of a change) and on the spouse (file a statement), it gives the Minister powers to waive and to direct,
-- and it says in what circumstances a supplement is calculated "as though the person had" or "did not have" a spouse
-- or common-law partner "on the last day of the previous payment period". The duties and powers are BOOLEAN rules over
-- the facts the section names. The third kind is the one that moves money: each such circumstance is a rule that says,
-- for a month, whether the supplement is calculated with a spouse (With) or without (Without), or that it does not
-- operate for that month (NOTHING). `s 15: the treatment that the directions and deemings give for the month` puts
-- them together and answers NOTHING when none operates or when two disagree (fork F-15-1: the Act ranks no
-- direction above another).
-- Judgments that the Act leaves to the Minister (is satisfied, directs) are facts the caller states.

§ `Part II -- Monthly Guaranteed Income Supplement`

§§ `Spouses and common-law partners, section 15`

-- (1) "Every person by whom an application for a supplement in respect of a payment period is made shall, in the
-- application, state whether the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner at any time during the payment
-- period or in the month before the first month of the payment period, and, if so, the name and address of the
-- spouse or common-law partner and whether, to the person's knowledge, the spouse or common-law partner is a
-- pensioner."
-- src:432 | 15 (1) Every person by whom an application for a supplement in respect of a payment period is made shall, in the application, state whether the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner at any time during the payment period or in the month before the first month of the payment period, and, if so, the name and address of the spouse or common-law partner and whether, to the person’s knowledge, the spouse or common-law partner is a pensioner.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(1) (src:432)
GIVEN `an application for a supplement in respect of a payment period is made by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(1): the person must state in the application whether the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner and, if so, who` `an application for a supplement in respect of a payment period is made by the person` MEANS
    `an application for a supplement in respect of a payment period is made by the person`

-- Whether the person "has or had a spouse or common-law partner at any time during the payment period or in the month
-- before the first month of the payment period": the days on which the person had a spouse or common-law partner are
-- the input; the rule asks whether any lies in the window.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(1) "at any time during the payment period or in the month before the first month of the payment period" (src:432)
GIVEN `the payment period` IS A `Calendar span`
      `a day on which the person had a spouse or common-law partner` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(1): the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner at a time in the window` `the payment period` `a day on which the person had a spouse or common-law partner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `a day on which the person had a spouse or common-law partner`
    WHEN JUST d THEN
            d AT LEAST `the first day of the month that is` (0 MINUS 1) `months after the month containing` (`the payment period`'s `first day`)
        AND d AT MOST `the payment period`'s `last day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- (1.1) "If the requirement for an application for payment of a supplement for any month has been waived under
-- subsection 11(4) for a person who did not have a spouse or common-law partner immediately before the last payment
-- period in respect of which a supplement was paid [...] but who has a spouse or common-law partner immediately
-- before the current payment period, the person shall notify the Minister without delay of the date of that change,
-- the name and address of the spouse or common-law partner and whether [...] the spouse or common-law partner is a
-- pensioner."
-- src:434 | (1.1) If the requirement for an application for payment of a supplement for any month has been waived under subsection 11(4) for a person who did not have a spouse or common-law partner immediately before the last payment period in respect of which a supplement was paid or, if no supplement was ever paid to the person, immediately before the last payment period in respect of which an application for payment of a supplement was received but who has a spouse or common-law partner immediately before the current payment period, the person shall notify the Minister without delay of the date of that change, the name and address of the spouse or common-law partner and whether, to the person’s knowledge, the spouse or common-law partner is a pensioner.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(1.1) (src:434)
GIVEN `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 11(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner immediately before the last payment period in respect of which a supplement was paid or, if none was ever paid, an application received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a spouse or common-law partner immediately before the current payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(1.1): the person must notify the Minister without delay of the change` `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 11(4)` `the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner immediately before the last payment period in respect of which a supplement was paid or, if none was ever paid, an application received` `the person has a spouse or common-law partner immediately before the current payment period` MEANS
        `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 11(4)`
    AND `the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner immediately before the last payment period in respect of which a supplement was paid or, if none was ever paid, an application received`
    AND `the person has a spouse or common-law partner immediately before the current payment period`

-- (3) The two grounds of a direction: (a) "no application or statement as described in subsection (2) has been filed
-- by or received from the spouse or common-law partner of the person and no estimate of the income of the spouse or
-- common-law partner of the person has been made under subsection 14(1.1)"; (b) "the Minister is satisfied that the
-- person, as a result of circumstances not attributable to the person or the spouse or common-law partner, was not
-- living with the spouse or common-law partner in a dwelling maintained by the person or the spouse or common-law
-- partner at the time the application was made".
-- src:450 | (a) no application or statement as described in subsection (2) has been filed by or received from the spouse or common-law partner of the person and no estimate of the income of the spouse or common-law partner of the person has been made under subsection 14(1.1); or
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(3)(a) (src:450)
GIVEN `an application or statement as described in subsection 15(2) has been filed by or received from the spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the income of the spouse or common-law partner has been estimated under subsection 14(1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(3)(a): the Minister may direct that the application be dealt with as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner` `an application or statement as described in subsection 15(2) has been filed by or received from the spouse or common-law partner` `the income of the spouse or common-law partner has been estimated under subsection 14(1.1)` MEANS
        NOT `an application or statement as described in subsection 15(2) has been filed by or received from the spouse or common-law partner`
    AND NOT `the income of the spouse or common-law partner has been estimated under subsection 14(1.1)`

-- src:451 | (b) the Minister is satisfied that the person, as a result of circumstances not attributable to the person or the spouse or common-law partner, was not living with the spouse or common-law partner in a dwelling maintained by the person or the spouse or common-law partner at the time the application was made.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(3)(b) (src:451)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that the person, as a result of circumstances not attributable to the person or the spouse or common-law partner, was not living with the spouse or common-law partner in a dwelling maintained by either of them at the time the application was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(3)(b): the Minister may direct that the application be dealt with as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner` `the Minister is satisfied that the person, as a result of circumstances not attributable to the person or the spouse or common-law partner, was not living with the spouse or common-law partner in a dwelling maintained by either of them at the time the application was made` MEANS
    `the Minister is satisfied that the person, as a result of circumstances not attributable to the person or the spouse or common-law partner, was not living with the spouse or common-law partner in a dwelling maintained by either of them at the time the application was made`

-- How a supplement is calculated while a direction or a deeming operates: "as though the person had a spouse or
-- common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period" (With) or "did not have" one (Without).
DECLARE `s 15: Treatment of the applicant's marital status in the calculation` IS ONE OF
    `s 15: as though the person had a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`
    `s 15: as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`

-- (3) and (3.1): "the Minister may [...] direct that the application be considered and dealt with as though the person
-- did not have a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period"; "A direction made
-- under subsection (3) in respect of a payment period is deemed to be a direction made in respect of every
-- subsequent payment period, but the Minister may [...] cancel the direction."
-- src:449 | (3) Where an application for a supplement in respect of any payment period has been made by a person, the Minister may, after any investigation of the circumstances that the Minister considers necessary, direct that the application be considered and dealt with as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period, in any case where
-- src:450 | (a) no application or statement as described in subsection (2) has been filed by or received from the spouse or common-law partner of the person and no estimate of the income of the spouse or common-law partner of the person has been made under subsection 14(1.1); or
-- src:451 | (b) the Minister is satisfied that the person, as a result of circumstances not attributable to the person or the spouse or common-law partner, was not living with the spouse or common-law partner in a dwelling maintained by the person or the spouse or common-law partner at the time the application was made.
-- src:452 | Continuing direction
-- src:453 | (3.1) A direction made under subsection (3) in respect of a payment period is deemed to be a direction made in respect of every subsequent payment period, but the Minister may, after any investigation of the circumstances that the Minister considers necessary, cancel the direction.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(3), s 15(3.1) (src:449-453)
GIVEN `a month for which the supplement is calculated` IS A DATE
      `a month in the payment period in respect of which the direction under subsection 15(3) was made (any date if none was made)` IS A DATE
      `a direction has been made under subsection 15(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction has been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 15: Treatment of the applicant's marital status in the calculation`
`s 15(3.1): the treatment under a continuing direction` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` `a month in the payment period in respect of which the direction under subsection 15(3) was made (any date if none was made)` `a direction has been made under subsection 15(3)` `the direction has been cancelled` MEANS
    IF     `a direction has been made under subsection 15(3)`
       AND NOT `the direction has been cancelled`
       AND (`the payment period in relation to the month containing` `a month for which the supplement is calculated`)'s `first day` AT LEAST (`the payment period in relation to the month containing` `a month in the payment period in respect of which the direction under subsection 15(3) was made (any date if none was made)`)'s `first day`
    THEN JUST `s 15: as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (3.2) "The Minister may [...] direct, in respect of any month in a payment period, that an application for a
-- supplement be considered and dealt with as though the applicant did not have a spouse or common-law partner on the
-- last day of the previous payment period if the Minister is satisfied that, at any time during the preceding month,
-- the applicant was the spouse or common-law partner of an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3), except
-- for the month in which the applicant's spouse or common-law partner is released."
-- src:455 | (3.2) The Minister may, after any investigation that the Minister considers necessary, direct, in respect of any month in a payment period, that an application for a supplement be considered and dealt with as though the applicant did not have a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period if the Minister is satisfied that, at any time during the preceding month, the applicant was the spouse or common-law partner of an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3), except for the month in which the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner is released.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(3.2) (src:455)
GIVEN `a month for which the supplement is calculated` IS A DATE
      `the Minister is satisfied that, at any time during the preceding month, the applicant was the spouse or common-law partner of an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: section 5(3) (piece oa1)
      `the month in which the applicant's spouse or common-law partner is released` IS A MAYBE DATE     -- out of range: section 5(3) (piece oa1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(3.2): the Minister may direct that the application be dealt with, for the month, as though the applicant did not have a spouse or common-law partner` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` `the Minister is satisfied that, at any time during the preceding month, the applicant was the spouse or common-law partner of an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` `the month in which the applicant's spouse or common-law partner is released` MEANS
        `the Minister is satisfied that, at any time during the preceding month, the applicant was the spouse or common-law partner of an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)`
    AND CONSIDER `the month in which the applicant's spouse or common-law partner is released`
        WHEN JUST released THEN NOT (`the first day of the month containing` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` EQUALS `the first day of the month containing` released)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

-- (3.3) "A direction made under subsection (3.2) continues to apply in respect of every subsequent month until the
-- month before the month in which the spouse or common-law partner is released. However, the Minister may [...]
-- cancel the direction."
-- src:457 | (3.3) A direction made under subsection (3.2) continues to apply in respect of every subsequent month until the month before the month in which the spouse or common-law partner is released. However, the Minister may, after any investigation of the circumstances that the Minister considers necessary, cancel the direction.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(3.3) (src:457)
GIVEN `a month for which the supplement is calculated` IS A DATE
      `the first month in respect of which a direction was made under subsection 15(3.2) (any date if none was made)` IS A DATE
      `a direction has been made under subsection 15(3.2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction has been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the applicant's spouse or common-law partner is released` IS A MAYBE DATE     -- out of range: section 5(3) (piece oa1)
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 15: Treatment of the applicant's marital status in the calculation`
`s 15(3.3): the treatment under a continuing direction for an incarcerated person's spouse or common-law partner` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` `the first month in respect of which a direction was made under subsection 15(3.2) (any date if none was made)` `a direction has been made under subsection 15(3.2)` `the direction has been cancelled` `the month in which the applicant's spouse or common-law partner is released` MEANS
    IF     `a direction has been made under subsection 15(3.2)`
       AND NOT `the direction has been cancelled`
       AND `the first day of the month containing` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` AT LEAST `the first day of the month containing` `the first month in respect of which a direction was made under subsection 15(3.2) (any date if none was made)`
       AND CONSIDER `the month in which the applicant's spouse or common-law partner is released`
           WHEN JUST released THEN `the first day of the month containing` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` LESS THAN `the first day of the month containing` released
           WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    THEN JUST `s 15: as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4.1) "Where an application for a supplement in respect of a payment period that commences after June 30, 1999 has
-- been made by a person, the Minister, if satisfied that the person is separated from the person's spouse, having
-- been so separated for a continuous period of at least three months, exclusive of the month in which the spouses
-- became separated, shall direct that the application be considered and dealt with as though the person had ceased to
-- have a spouse at the end of the third such month."
-- So a month after the third month after the month of separation is calculated without a spouse (with (7.1)).
-- src:461 | (4.1) Where an application for a supplement in respect of a payment period that commences after June 30, 1999 has been made by a person, the Minister, if satisfied that the person is separated from the person’s spouse, having been so separated for a continuous period of at least three months, exclusive of the month in which the spouses became separated, shall direct that the application be considered and dealt with as though the person had ceased to have a spouse at the end of the third such month.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(4.1) (src:461)
GIVEN `a month for which the supplement is calculated` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the payment period in respect of which the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the Minister is satisfied that the person is separated from the person's spouse, having been so separated for a continuous period of at least three months, exclusive of the month in which the spouses became separated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the spouses became separated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 15: Treatment of the applicant's marital status in the calculation`
`s 15(4.1): the treatment for a separated person` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` `the first day of the payment period in respect of which the application is made` `the Minister is satisfied that the person is separated from the person's spouse, having been so separated for a continuous period of at least three months, exclusive of the month in which the spouses became separated` `the month in which the spouses became separated` MEANS
    IF     `the first day of the payment period in respect of which the application is made` GREATER THAN (YMD 1999 6 30)
       AND `the Minister is satisfied that the person is separated from the person's spouse, having been so separated for a continuous period of at least three months, exclusive of the month in which the spouses became separated`
       AND `the first day of the month containing` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` GREATER THAN `the first day of the month that is` 3 `months after the month containing` `the month in which the spouses became separated`
    THEN JUST `s 15: as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4.2) "Where an application for a supplement in respect of a payment period that commences after June 30, 1999 is
-- made by a person who at any time in the payment period ceases to have a common-law partner otherwise than by
-- reason of the common-law partner's death, the supplement paid to the person, for any month in that payment period
-- after the third month following the month in which the person ceased to have a common-law partner, shall be
-- calculated as though the person did not have a common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period."
-- src:463 | (4.2) Where an application for a supplement in respect of a payment period that commences after June 30, 1999 is made by a person who at any time in the payment period ceases to have a common-law partner otherwise than by reason of the common-law partner’s death, the supplement paid to the person, for any month in that payment period after the third month following the month in which the person ceased to have a common-law partner, shall be calculated as though the person did not have a common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(4.2) (src:463)
GIVEN `a month for which the supplement is calculated` IS A DATE
      `the payment period in respect of which the application is made` IS A `Calendar span`
      `the month in which the person ceased to have a common-law partner otherwise than by reason of the common-law partner's death (any date if none)` IS A DATE
      `the person ceased to have a common-law partner otherwise than by reason of the common-law partner's death at a time in the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 15: Treatment of the applicant's marital status in the calculation`
`s 15(4.2): the treatment after a common-law partner is lost otherwise than by death` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` `the payment period in respect of which the application is made` `the month in which the person ceased to have a common-law partner otherwise than by reason of the common-law partner's death (any date if none)` `the person ceased to have a common-law partner otherwise than by reason of the common-law partner's death at a time in the payment period` MEANS
    IF     `the payment period in respect of which the application is made`'s `first day` GREATER THAN (YMD 1999 6 30)
       AND `the person ceased to have a common-law partner otherwise than by reason of the common-law partner's death at a time in the payment period`
       AND `the first day of the month containing` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` AT LEAST `the payment period in respect of which the application is made`'s `first day`
       AND `the first day of the month containing` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` AT MOST `the payment period in respect of which the application is made`'s `last day`
       AND `the first day of the month containing` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` GREATER THAN `the first day of the month that is` 3 `months after the month containing` `the month in which the person ceased to have a common-law partner otherwise than by reason of the common-law partner's death (any date if none)`
    THEN JUST `s 15: as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (5) For a payment period that ends before July 1, 1999, "the Minister may review the direction previously made
-- and direct that any supplement paid [...] for any month in that payment period after the month in which the review
-- is made be calculated either on the basis that the applicant and the spouse or common-law partner were spouses or
-- common-law partners of each other on the last day of the previous payment period or as though they had not been
-- spouses or common-law partners on that day, according as the direction may specify."
-- src:465 | (5) Where, after the Minister has made a direction under subsection (3) with respect to an application for a supplement made in respect of a payment period that ends before July 1, 1999, a statement or application as described in subsection (2) is filed by or received from the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner, the Minister may review the direction previously made and direct that any supplement paid to the applicant or the spouse or common-law partner for any month in that payment period after the month in which the review is made be calculated either on the basis that the applicant and the spouse or common-law partner were spouses or common-law partners of each other on the last day of the previous payment period or as though they had not been spouses or common-law partners on that day, according as the direction may specify.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(5) (src:465)
GIVEN `a month for which the supplement is calculated` IS A DATE
      `the payment period in respect of which the application was made` IS A `Calendar span`
      `the Minister has reviewed a direction under subsection 15(3) after a statement or application as described in subsection 15(2) was filed or received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the review is made` IS A DATE
      `the basis the direction specifies` IS A MAYBE `s 15: Treatment of the applicant's marital status in the calculation`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 15: Treatment of the applicant's marital status in the calculation`
`s 15(5): the treatment under a reviewed direction for a payment period ending before July 1, 1999` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` `the payment period in respect of which the application was made` `the Minister has reviewed a direction under subsection 15(3) after a statement or application as described in subsection 15(2) was filed or received` `the month in which the review is made` `the basis the direction specifies` MEANS
    IF     `the payment period in respect of which the application was made`'s `last day` LESS THAN (YMD 1999 7 1)
       AND `the Minister has reviewed a direction under subsection 15(3) after a statement or application as described in subsection 15(2) was filed or received`
       AND `the first day of the month containing` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` GREATER THAN `the first day of the month containing` `the month in which the review is made`
       AND `the first day of the month containing` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` AT MOST `the payment period in respect of which the application was made`'s `last day`
    THEN `the basis the direction specifies`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (5.1) "Where, after the Minister has made a direction under subsection (3) based on paragraph (3)(a), with respect
-- to an application for a supplement made in respect of a payment period that commences after June 30, 1999 and a
-- statement or application as described in subsection (2) is filed by or received from the applicant's spouse or
-- common-law partner, the Minister shall review the direction previously made and shall direct that any supplement
-- paid to the applicant or the spouse or common-law partner for months in that payment period after the month in
-- which the review is completed be calculated on the basis that the applicant and the spouse or common-law partner
-- were spouses or common-law partners of each other on the last day of the previous payment period, unless there is
-- some other reason for a direction to be made under subsection (3)."
-- src:467 | (5.1) Where, after the Minister has made a direction under subsection (3) based on paragraph (3)(a), with respect to an application for a supplement made in respect of a payment period that commences after June 30, 1999 and a statement or application as described in subsection (2) is filed by or received from the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner, the Minister shall review the direction previously made and shall direct that any supplement paid to the applicant or the spouse or common-law partner for months in that payment period after the month in which the review is completed be calculated on the basis that the applicant and the spouse or common-law partner were spouses or common-law partners of each other on the last day of the previous payment period, unless there is some other reason for a direction to be made under subsection (3).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(5.1) (src:467)
GIVEN `a month for which the supplement is calculated` IS A DATE
      `the payment period in respect of which the application was made` IS A `Calendar span`
      `a direction was made under subsection 15(3) based on paragraph 15(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement or application as described in subsection 15(2) was later filed by or received from the spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is some other reason for a direction to be made under subsection 15(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the review is completed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 15: Treatment of the applicant's marital status in the calculation`
`s 15(5.1): the treatment after the review of a direction` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` `the payment period in respect of which the application was made` `a direction was made under subsection 15(3) based on paragraph 15(3)(a)` `a statement or application as described in subsection 15(2) was later filed by or received from the spouse or common-law partner` `there is some other reason for a direction to be made under subsection 15(3)` `the month in which the review is completed` MEANS
    IF     `the payment period in respect of which the application was made`'s `first day` GREATER THAN (YMD 1999 6 30)
       AND `a direction was made under subsection 15(3) based on paragraph 15(3)(a)`
       AND `a statement or application as described in subsection 15(2) was later filed by or received from the spouse or common-law partner`
       AND NOT `there is some other reason for a direction to be made under subsection 15(3)`
       AND `the first day of the month containing` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` GREATER THAN `the first day of the month containing` `the month in which the review is completed`
       AND `the first day of the month containing` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` AT MOST `the payment period in respect of which the application was made`'s `last day`
    THEN JUST `s 15: as though the person had a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (6.1) "Where an application for a supplement in respect of a payment period that commences after June 30, 1999 is
-- made by (a) a person who did not have a spouse or common-law partner immediately before a particular month in the
-- payment period but has a spouse or common-law partner at the end of that month, (b) a person in respect of whom a
-- direction is made under subsection (3) based on paragraph (3)(b) who no longer meets the conditions set out in that
-- paragraph, or (c) a person described in subsection (4.1) who ceases to be separated from the person's spouse, the
-- calculation of the supplement shall be made, for any month after the month in which the person began to have a
-- spouse or common-law partner, as though the person had a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the
-- previous payment period."
-- src:470 | (6.1) Where an application for a supplement in respect of a payment period that commences after June 30, 1999 is made by
-- src:471 | (a) a person who did not have a spouse or common-law partner immediately before a particular month in the payment period but has a spouse or common-law partner at the end of that month,
-- src:472 | (b) a person in respect of whom a direction is made under subsection (3) based on paragraph (3)(b) who no longer meets the conditions set out in that paragraph, or
-- src:473 | (c) a person described in subsection (4.1) who ceases to be separated from the person’s spouse,
-- src:474 | the calculation of the supplement shall be made, for any month after the month in which the person began to have a spouse or common-law partner, as though the person had a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(6.1) (src:470-474)
GIVEN `a month for which the supplement is calculated` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the payment period in respect of which the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner immediately before a particular month in the payment period but has a spouse or common-law partner at the end of that month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person in respect of whom a direction is made under subsection 15(3) based on paragraph 15(3)(b) who no longer meets the conditions set out in that paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person described in subsection 15(4.1) who ceases to be separated from the person's spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the person began to have a spouse or common-law partner` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 15: Treatment of the applicant's marital status in the calculation`
`s 15(6.1): the treatment after a person begins to have a spouse or common-law partner` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` `the first day of the payment period in respect of which the application is made` `the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner immediately before a particular month in the payment period but has a spouse or common-law partner at the end of that month` `the person is a person in respect of whom a direction is made under subsection 15(3) based on paragraph 15(3)(b) who no longer meets the conditions set out in that paragraph` `the person is a person described in subsection 15(4.1) who ceases to be separated from the person's spouse` `the month in which the person began to have a spouse or common-law partner` MEANS
    IF     `the first day of the payment period in respect of which the application is made` GREATER THAN (YMD 1999 6 30)
       AND (   `the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner immediately before a particular month in the payment period but has a spouse or common-law partner at the end of that month`
            OR `the person is a person in respect of whom a direction is made under subsection 15(3) based on paragraph 15(3)(b) who no longer meets the conditions set out in that paragraph`
            OR `the person is a person described in subsection 15(4.1) who ceases to be separated from the person's spouse`)
       AND `the first day of the month containing` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` GREATER THAN `the first day of the month containing` `the month in which the person began to have a spouse or common-law partner`
    THEN JUST `s 15: as though the person had a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (7.1) "Where an application for a supplement in respect of a payment period that commences after June 30, 1999 is
-- made by a person who at any time in the payment period ceases to have a spouse, the supplement paid to the person,
-- for any month in that payment period after the month in which the person ceased to have a spouse, shall be
-- calculated as though the person did not have a spouse on the last day of the previous payment period."
-- src:477 | (7.1) Where an application for a supplement in respect of a payment period that commences after June 30, 1999 is made by a person who at any time in the payment period ceases to have a spouse, the supplement paid to the person, for any month in that payment period after the month in which the person ceased to have a spouse, shall be calculated as though the person did not have a spouse on the last day of the previous payment period.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(7.1) (src:477)
GIVEN `a month for which the supplement is calculated` IS A DATE
      `the payment period in respect of which the application is made` IS A `Calendar span`
      `the person ceased to have a spouse at a time in the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the person ceased to have a spouse` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 15: Treatment of the applicant's marital status in the calculation`
`s 15(7.1): the treatment after a person ceases to have a spouse` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` `the payment period in respect of which the application is made` `the person ceased to have a spouse at a time in the payment period` `the month in which the person ceased to have a spouse` MEANS
    IF     `the payment period in respect of which the application is made`'s `first day` GREATER THAN (YMD 1999 6 30)
       AND `the person ceased to have a spouse at a time in the payment period`
       AND `the first day of the month containing` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` GREATER THAN `the first day of the month containing` `the month in which the person ceased to have a spouse`
       AND `the first day of the month containing` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` AT MOST `the payment period in respect of which the application is made`'s `last day`
    THEN JUST `s 15: as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (7.2) The same where the person ceases to have a common-law partner by reason of the common-law partner's death:
-- "for any month in that payment period after the month in which the common-law partner died".
-- src:479 | (7.2) Where an application for a supplement in respect of a payment period that commences after June 30, 1999 is made by a person who at any time in the payment period ceases to have a common-law partner by reason of the common-law partner’s death, the supplement paid to the person, for any month in that payment period after the month in which the common-law partner died, shall be calculated as though the person did not have a common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(7.2) (src:479)
GIVEN `a month for which the supplement is calculated` IS A DATE
      `the payment period in respect of which the application is made` IS A `Calendar span`
      `the person ceased to have a common-law partner by reason of the common-law partner's death at a time in the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the common-law partner died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 15: Treatment of the applicant's marital status in the calculation`
`s 15(7.2): the treatment after a common-law partner dies` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` `the payment period in respect of which the application is made` `the person ceased to have a common-law partner by reason of the common-law partner's death at a time in the payment period` `the month in which the common-law partner died` MEANS
    IF     `the payment period in respect of which the application is made`'s `first day` GREATER THAN (YMD 1999 6 30)
       AND `the person ceased to have a common-law partner by reason of the common-law partner's death at a time in the payment period`
       AND `the first day of the month containing` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` GREATER THAN `the first day of the month containing` `the month in which the common-law partner died`
       AND `the first day of the month containing` `a month for which the supplement is calculated` AT MOST `the payment period in respect of which the application is made`'s `last day`
    THEN JUST `s 15: as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Fork F-15-1: the Act says (8) that subsections (6.1) to (7.2) do not limit the Minister's authority to make a
-- direction under subsections (3) to (5.1), and does not say which prevails when a direction and a deeming give
-- different answers for a month. The rules above give the answers they give; this one adds them up and answers
-- NOTHING, rather than choosing, when two disagree or none operates.
-- src:481 | (8) Nothing in subsections (6.1) to (7.2) shall be construed as limiting or restricting the authority of the Minister to make a direction under subsections (3) to (5.1).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(8) and fork F-15-1 (src:481)
GIVEN treatments IS A LIST OF MAYBE `s 15: Treatment of the applicant's marital status in the calculation`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 15: Treatment of the applicant's marital status in the calculation`
`s 15: the treatment that the directions and deemings give for the month` treatments MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF hasWith AND NOT hasWithout THEN JUST `s 15: as though the person had a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`
        IF hasWithout AND NOT hasWith THEN JUST `s 15: as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        hasWith MEANS any (GIVEN t YIELD t EQUALS JUST `s 15: as though the person had a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`) treatments
        hasWithout MEANS any (GIVEN t YIELD t EQUALS JUST `s 15: as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`) treatments

-- (2) "Subject to subsections (3), (4.1) and (4.2), where a person makes an application for a supplement in respect
-- of a payment period and the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner at any time during the payment period
-- or in the month before the first month of the payment period, the application shall not be considered or dealt
-- with until such time as (a) the applicant's spouse or common-law partner files a statement in prescribed form of
-- the spouse's or common-law partner's income for the base calendar year; (b) an application for a supplement in
-- respect of the current payment period is received from the applicant's spouse or common-law partner; or (c) the
-- income of the applicant's spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year is estimated under subsection
-- 14(1.1)." Read "Subject to (3), (4.1) and (4.2)" as: where a direction under (3) or (4.1) has been made, or (4.2)
-- applies, the application may be considered without waiting (fork F-15-2).
-- src:436 | (2) Subject to subsections (3), (4.1) and (4.2), where a person makes an application for a supplement in respect of a payment period and the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner at any time during the payment period or in the month before the first month of the payment period, the application shall not be considered or dealt with until such time as
-- src:437 | (a) the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner files a statement in prescribed form of the spouse’s or common-law partner’s income for the base calendar year;
-- src:438 | (b) an application for a supplement in respect of the current payment period is received from the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner; or
-- src:439 | (c) the income of the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year is estimated under subsection 14(1.1).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(2) (src:436-439)
GIVEN `the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner at any time during the payment period or in the month before the first month of the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the spouse or common-law partner has filed a statement in prescribed form of the spouse's or common-law partner's income for the base calendar year` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: section 35, the form of a statement (piece oa1)
      `an application for a supplement in respect of the current payment period has been received from the spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the income of the spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year has been estimated under subsection 14(1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a direction under subsection 15(3) has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a direction under subsection 15(4.1) has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 15(4.2) applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(2): the application may be considered and dealt with` `the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner at any time during the payment period or in the month before the first month of the payment period` `the spouse or common-law partner has filed a statement in prescribed form of the spouse's or common-law partner's income for the base calendar year` `an application for a supplement in respect of the current payment period has been received from the spouse or common-law partner` `the income of the spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year has been estimated under subsection 14(1.1)` `a direction under subsection 15(3) has been made` `a direction under subsection 15(4.1) has been made` `subsection 15(4.2) applies to the person` MEANS
       NOT `the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner at any time during the payment period or in the month before the first month of the payment period`
    OR `the spouse or common-law partner has filed a statement in prescribed form of the spouse's or common-law partner's income for the base calendar year`
    OR `an application for a supplement in respect of the current payment period has been received from the spouse or common-law partner`
    OR `the income of the spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year has been estimated under subsection 14(1.1)`
    OR `a direction under subsection 15(3) has been made`
    OR `a direction under subsection 15(4.1) has been made`
    OR `subsection 15(4.2) applies to the person`

-- (2.1) "The Minister may waive the requirement to submit the information described in subsection (1) if that
-- information has been submitted to the Minister in a joint application referred to in subsection 19(4)."
-- src:441 | (2.1) The Minister may waive the requirement to submit the information described in subsection (1) if that information has been submitted to the Minister in a joint application referred to in subsection 19(4).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(2.1) (src:441)
GIVEN `the information has been submitted to the Minister in a joint application referred to in subsection 19(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(2.1): the Minister may waive the requirement to submit the information described in subsection 15(1)` `the information has been submitted to the Minister in a joint application referred to in subsection 19(4)` MEANS
    `the information has been submitted to the Minister in a joint application referred to in subsection 19(4)`

-- (2.2) "The Minister may waive the requirement to file a statement under paragraph (2)(a) if the information has been
-- made available to the Minister under this Act, and, if that is the case, the statement is deemed to have been filed
-- for the purposes of this Part."
-- src:443 | (2.2) The Minister may waive the requirement to file a statement under paragraph (2)(a) if the information has been made available to the Minister under this Act, and, if that is the case, the statement is deemed to have been filed for the purposes of this Part.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(2.2) (src:443)
GIVEN `the information has been made available to the Minister under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(2.2): the Minister may waive the requirement to file a statement under paragraph 15(2)(a)` `the information has been made available to the Minister under this Act` MEANS
    `the information has been made available to the Minister under this Act`

@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(2.2) "the statement is deemed to have been filed" (src:443)
GIVEN `the spouse or common-law partner has filed a statement in prescribed form of the spouse's or common-law partner's income for the base calendar year` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: section 35, the form of a statement (piece oa1)
      `the Minister has waived the requirement to file the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(2.2): the statement is filed or is deemed to have been filed` `the spouse or common-law partner has filed a statement in prescribed form of the spouse's or common-law partner's income for the base calendar year` `the Minister has waived the requirement to file the statement` MEANS
    `the spouse or common-law partner has filed a statement in prescribed form of the spouse's or common-law partner's income for the base calendar year` OR `the Minister has waived the requirement to file the statement`

-- (2.3) "If the Minister intends to waive the requirement for an application in respect of a person under subsection
-- 11(3.1) and the person has a spouse or common-law partner, the Minister shall notify the spouse or common-law
-- partner in writing of that intention and provide the spouse or common-law partner with the information regarding
-- them on which the Minister intends to rely to approve the payment of a supplement."
-- src:445 | (2.3) If the Minister intends to waive the requirement for an application in respect of a person under subsection 11(3.1) and the person has a spouse or common-law partner, the Minister shall notify the spouse or common-law partner in writing of that intention and provide the spouse or common-law partner with the information regarding them on which the Minister intends to rely to approve the payment of a supplement.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(2.3) (src:445)
GIVEN `the Minister intends to waive the requirement for an application in respect of the person under subsection 11(3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(2.3): the Minister must notify the spouse or common-law partner in writing and provide the information` `the Minister intends to waive the requirement for an application in respect of the person under subsection 11(3.1)` `the person has a spouse or common-law partner` MEANS
    `the Minister intends to waive the requirement for an application in respect of the person under subsection 11(3.1)` AND `the person has a spouse or common-law partner`

-- (2.4) "The person's spouse or common-law partner shall, before the day on which the person attains 65 years of age,
-- file with the Minister a statement in which the spouse or common-law partner corrects any inaccuracies in the
-- information provided by the Minister under subsection (2.3)." The last day is the day before the 65th birthday.
-- src:447 | (2.4) The person’s spouse or common-law partner shall, before the day on which the person attains 65 years of age, file with the Minister a statement in which the spouse or common-law partner corrects any inaccuracies in the information provided by the Minister under subsection (2.3).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(2.4) (src:447)
GIVEN `the person's date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 15(2.4): the last day on which the spouse or common-law partner may file the statement correcting inaccuracies` `the person's date of birth` MEANS
    `the day that is` (`a limit in days` 1) `before` (`the day on which a person born on` `the person's date of birth` `attains the age of` 65)

@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(2.4) (src:447)
GIVEN `the information provided by the Minister under subsection 15(2.3) contains inaccuracies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the spouse or common-law partner files the statement` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the person's date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(2.4): the spouse or common-law partner has complied with the duty to file a statement correcting inaccuracies` `the information provided by the Minister under subsection 15(2.3) contains inaccuracies` `the day on which the spouse or common-law partner files the statement` `the person's date of birth` MEANS
    NOT `the information provided by the Minister under subsection 15(2.3) contains inaccuracies`
    OR CONSIDER `the day on which the spouse or common-law partner files the statement`
       WHEN JUST d THEN d AT MOST `s 15(2.4): the last day on which the spouse or common-law partner may file the statement correcting inaccuracies` `the person's date of birth`
       WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- (4) "Every applicant who is the subject of a direction under subsection (3.2) shall inform the Minister without
-- delay of their spouse or common-law partner's release."
-- src:459 | (4) Every applicant who is the subject of a direction under subsection (3.2) shall inform the Minister without delay of their spouse or common-law partner’s release.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(4) (src:459)
GIVEN `the applicant is the subject of a direction under subsection 15(3.2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(4): the applicant must inform the Minister without delay of the release` `the applicant is the subject of a direction under subsection 15(3.2)` MEANS
    `the applicant is the subject of a direction under subsection 15(3.2)`

-- (9) "Every applicant shall inform the Minister without delay if they separate from, or cease to have, a spouse or
-- common-law partner, or if they had a spouse or common-law partner at the beginning of a month, not having had a
-- spouse or common-law partner at the beginning of the previous month."
-- src:483 | (9) Every applicant shall inform the Minister without delay if they separate from, or cease to have, a spouse or common-law partner, or if they had a spouse or common-law partner at the beginning of a month, not having had a spouse or common-law partner at the beginning of the previous month.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 15(9) (src:483)
GIVEN `the applicant separates from a spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant ceases to have a spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant had a spouse or common-law partner at the beginning of a month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant did not have a spouse or common-law partner at the beginning of the previous month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15(9): the applicant must inform the Minister without delay` `the applicant separates from a spouse or common-law partner` `the applicant ceases to have a spouse or common-law partner` `the applicant had a spouse or common-law partner at the beginning of a month` `the applicant did not have a spouse or common-law partner at the beginning of the previous month` MEANS
       `the applicant separates from a spouse or common-law partner`
    OR `the applicant ceases to have a spouse or common-law partner`
    OR (   `the applicant had a spouse or common-law partner at the beginning of a month`
       AND `the applicant did not have a spouse or common-law partner at the beginning of the previous month`)
